{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ColourWeightHullThreshold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ColourWeightHullThreshold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.hull_bound_fails_beyond_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.hull_bound_fails_beyond_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L103-L109","doc":"Non-vacuity: the threshold is sharp.  At `δ = 4` the weight on `σ⁻¹` is\n`−1/2`, and the combination `(3/2)·1 + (−1/2)·0 = 3/2` exceeds both endpoints —\nso beyond `|δ| = 2` the bound genuinely fails rather than merely losing its\nproof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.target_above_max_forces_outside_hull","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.target_above_max_forces_outside_hull","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L88-L101","doc":"**The converse that carries the physics.**  If an affine combination\nattains a value strictly greater than both endpoints, its weight lies outside\n`[0,1]`.  So a target above the branch ceiling cannot be reached by any\nadmissible colour weight — it is not a matter of choosing `δ` well. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.affine_le_max_of_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.affine_le_max_of_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L82-L86","doc":"Inside the hull, an affine combination of two values is at most their\nmaximum.  The two-point case of `convex_comb_le_bound`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colourWeights_nonneg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colourWeights_nonneg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L67-L80","doc":"**The threshold.**  Both weights are non-negative exactly when `|δ| ≤ 2`.\nBelow it the letter lies in the convex hull of `{σ, σ⁻¹}` and\n`convex_comb_le_bound` applies; above it one weight is negative and the bound\nhas no force. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.colourWeights_sum_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.colourWeights_sum_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The letter is an AFFINE combination for every `δ` — a consequence of\n`σ⁻¹ = σ − h`, not an assumption about the colour weighting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.wNeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.wNeg","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L59-L60","doc":"Weight on `σ⁻¹` in the colour-weighted p–n letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.wPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.wPos","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ColourWeightHullThreshold.lean#L56-L57","doc":"Weight on `σ` in the colour-weighted p–n letter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}